# Tier A's clang-tidy configuration (docs/phases/0-safety-net.md item 0.9).
#
# Scope: the checks that catch real defects in a migration that is moving code from
# Objective-C to C++ one translation unit at a time. Style checks are deliberately absent
# — the tree is 20 years of upstream Objective-C, and a Tier A that fires on every
# untouched line is a Tier A that agents learn to ignore.
#
# The exclusions below are all "true of the existing tree, not of this bead's edit".
# Removing one is a deliberate, separately-beaded tightening, not a drive-by.
#
#   bugprone-narrowing-conversions      pervasive in the float-heavy maths (Vector, OOColor).
#   bugprone-switch-missing-default-case  upstream style: exhaustive enum switches, no default.
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters  fires on every (x1,y1,x2,y2) geometry helper.
#   misc-no-recursion                   the OXP verifier and the plist parsers are recursive by design.
#   misc-const-correctness              upstream C/ObjC bodies assign once and never mark it (they
#                                        predate C++); it fires on every OOJS_RETURN_*/OOJS_BEGIN_FULL_NATIVE
#                                        macro expansion (JS_* retarget beads, ADR-0001/ADR-0002) and on
#                                        every other untouched local in a file newly compiled as
#                                        Objective-C++, not on anything a retarget bead wrote.
#
# Note the companion settings that live in tools/tier-a.sh rather than here, because they
# are about *where* we look rather than *what* we look for: -header-filter='$^' keeps
# diagnostics to the translation unit itself (a shared header would otherwise report the
# same finding once per TU that includes it), and --warnings-as-errors='*' is what makes a
# finding fail the tier.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  misc-*,
  performance-*,
  -bugprone-narrowing-conversions,
  -bugprone-switch-missing-default-case,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -misc-no-recursion,
  -misc-const-correctness

# Findings in headers are reported by the TU that owns them, not by every includer.
HeaderFilterRegex: '$^'

FormatStyle: none
